  "question": {
    "text": "If a line makes an angle of $\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ with the positive directions of each of $x$-axis and $y$-axis, then the angle that the line makes with the positive direction of the $z-$axis is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "dqA48",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{6}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DTkaR",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{3}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "YxrlL",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{4}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DgXrj",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{l}=\\cos \\frac{\\pi}{4}, m=\\cos \\frac{\\pi}{4}$\nwe know $\\mathrm{l}^2+\\mathrm{m}^2+\\mathrm{n}^2=1$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}+n^2=1 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow n=0\n\\end{aligned}$\nHence angle with positive direction of $\\mathrm{z-}$ axis is $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$.",
    "image": null
  },
